WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.020
<b>1969                            July 20th</b>

00:00:00.990 --> 00:00:03.520
<i>Space. It was long in the past that we,</i>

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:05.750
<i>humanity, had flown higher than the sky</i>

00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:07.360
<i>and set foot on the moon.</i>

00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:09.890
<i>We've even set out to travel</i>

00:00:09.890 --> 00:00:11.460
<i>outside of this solar system,</i>

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:13.570
<i>taking monumental journeys to 
the outer reaches of the universe.</i>

00:00:13.570 --> 00:00:15.490
<i>But what about the oceans?</i>

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:18.940
<i>We haven't even seen what it 
looks like a mere 10,000 meters</i>

00:00:18.940 --> 00:00:20.410
<i>below the water's surface.</i>

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:23.990
<i>Time, light, temperature...</i>

00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:28.140
<i>A deep, unknown realm that these things 
can't even come close to touching.</i>

00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:28.900
<i>The ocean.</i>

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:31.410
<i>The oceans, farther than the moon.</i>

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:34.320
<i>Sitting here like this,</i>

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:37.670
<i>hoping for a rare knock at the 
door to this world may be</i>

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:39.920
<i>what it means to go fishing.</i>

00:00:41.310 --> 00:00:42.600
<i>That being said...</i>

00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:47.020
<i>This isn't what I had hoped 
would come knocking!</i>

00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:48.730
Y-You must be tired.

00:00:49.880 --> 00:00:51.870
What is this?!

00:00:51.870 --> 00:00:52.850
What is it, what is it?

00:00:52.850 --> 00:00:55.160
Oh, that's a giant oarfish.

00:00:55.160 --> 00:00:55.900
Pretty rare.

00:00:55.900 --> 00:00:57.550
Muromi-san, you know him?

00:00:57.550 --> 00:00:59.700
I know most fish.

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:01.960
Huh? A giant oarfish?

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:03.890
That's right. King of the herrings.

00:01:03.890 --> 00:01:04.900
Work...

00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:06.370
Give me work.

00:01:06.370 --> 00:01:12.600
Ryuuguujou 
Memorial

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:09.700
I told you that the Ryuuguujou 
went out of business, right?

00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:12.590
Yeah, you did say it existed until recently...

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:15.210
He used to work at the Ryuuguujou castle,

00:01:15.210 --> 00:01:16.560
as "king of herrings" implies,

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:19.030
and he's been unemployed 
since the castle's been gone.

00:01:19.030 --> 00:01:20.770
The ocean's undergoing a recession too?

00:01:20.770 --> 00:01:22.600
Give me work. I'll do anything.

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:24.130
Get away!

00:01:25.450 --> 00:01:28.330
Takkun, do you know of any 
good job openings?

00:01:28.330 --> 00:01:29.370
Of course I don't!

00:01:29.370 --> 00:01:32.210
Like a student would know 
where to find a fish a job!

00:01:32.210 --> 00:01:33.530
Please, anything will do!

00:01:32.580 --> 00:01:33.530
I can't help you!

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:36.880
Why don't you help him, Muromi-san?

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:38.020
You're both fish, aren't you?

00:01:38.020 --> 00:01:40.300
I've already tried a bunch, 
and it hasn't worked.

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:41.770
That's why I'm asking you.

00:01:41.770 --> 00:01:44.700
I want... I want stability.

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:47.580
There's a boss of each section of the ocean,

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:50.200
so I was trying to get 
him to get us some work.

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:53.670
<i>You won't even be able to clean a 
coral reef with a body like that.</i>

00:01:53.670 --> 00:01:56.040
So he was completely turned down.

00:01:56.040 --> 00:01:57.850
<i>Why are you waving around like that?</i>

00:01:57.850 --> 00:01:59.130
<i>You don't really want work, do you?!</i>

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:00.930
The main reason is that

00:02:00.930 --> 00:02:04.170
I'm not sure what this 
guy does in his free time.

00:02:03.700 --> 00:02:05.090
Secretive?

00:02:04.170 --> 00:02:07.920
I guess it is a problem if you 
don't know what type of guy he is.

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:09.980
My private life is no one's business.

00:02:09.980 --> 00:02:11.290
Kids these days!

00:02:11.290 --> 00:02:15.200
I think it'd be advantageous if you 
had something you excelled in,

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:17.070
at least in the human world, anyway.

00:02:17.550 --> 00:02:18.860
Talent, huh?

00:02:18.860 --> 00:02:22.570
Oh! The oarfish do have a special ability.

00:02:22.570 --> 00:02:24.100
Oh? What is it?

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:30.750
Bossun

00:02:30.830 --> 00:02:32.160
What's going on?! What's going on?!

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:33.930
The blessing of rain!

00:02:33.930 --> 00:02:35.610
This is the oarfish's special ability.

00:02:35.610 --> 00:02:38.050
Whenever you catch one, a 
strange natural event occurs!

00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:40.380
So high up!

00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:41.020
Get back to...

00:02:41.020 --> 00:02:41.950
This isn't working.

00:02:41.950 --> 00:02:43.100
...the water!

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:45.810
Th-That was mean.

00:02:45.810 --> 00:02:48.270
The fixed-net fishermen always scowl,

00:02:48.270 --> 00:02:51.050
thinking they're bad luck 
when they catch one.

00:02:51.050 --> 00:02:53.220
They're not very liked by humans.

00:02:53.220 --> 00:02:54.520
That commentary wasn't needed!

00:02:55.700 --> 00:02:57.510
The rain's letting up.

00:02:57.510 --> 00:02:59.490
What an obnoxious ability.

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:02.050
Well, I guess you don't see them often,

00:03:02.050 --> 00:03:03.610
and with an ability like that, 
they don't have to worry

00:03:03.610 --> 00:03:05.110
about being overfished, I guess.

00:03:05.110 --> 00:03:07.700
It's not like he wanted that ability.

00:03:07.700 --> 00:03:11.210
It's more like a curse than a special ability.

00:03:12.030 --> 00:03:13.260
Curse?

00:03:13.260 --> 00:03:14.420
What do you mean, curse?

00:03:18.310 --> 00:03:19.870
Ryuuguu!

00:03:19.870 --> 00:03:20.980
Otohime's curse.

00:03:19.870 --> 00:03:22.060
I won't let you run away!

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:25.450
I want you to work like horses!

00:03:25.450 --> 00:03:26.540
She sounds awful!

00:03:26.540 --> 00:03:27.680
That's what she's like?

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:29.870
Urashima-kun was her victim too, wasn't he?

00:03:27.700 --> 00:03:30.890
<b>Tamatebako</b>

00:03:29.870 --> 00:03:30.890
She sounds pretty devious.

00:03:31.700 --> 00:03:33.990
I want to be of use to someone.

00:03:33.990 --> 00:03:35.880
I want to be needed.

00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:39.060
Good morning.

00:03:39.060 --> 00:03:40.130
It's the height of summer.

00:03:40.130 --> 00:03:41.570
How is everyone out there doing?

00:03:41.910 --> 00:03:43.470
It's time to look at today's weather.

00:03:43.470 --> 00:03:46.540
We had a sudden downpour yesterday 
in the Kantou region.

00:03:46.540 --> 00:03:48.410
We've had a lot of those lately, haven't we?

00:03:48.410 --> 00:03:49.290
What?

00:03:56.090 --> 00:04:00.420
<b>Muromi-san on the Shore</b>

00:03:56.090 --> 00:04:00.420
<b>Episode 6
"Muromi-san and Ryuuguujou"</b>

00:05:19.290 --> 00:05:24.920
<b>Bait & Tackle Period</b>

00:05:19.440 --> 00:05:21.490
Fishing isn't free.

00:05:21.490 --> 00:05:24.050
Like everything else in 
the world, it costs money.

00:05:24.050 --> 00:05:27.220
And when they sell things 
that make fishing easier...

00:05:24.920 --> 00:05:27.220
<b>Electric Reel</b>

00:05:27.600 --> 00:05:29.200
An electric reel, huh?

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:30.360
Pretty expensive.

00:05:30.360 --> 00:05:33.430
Would you like to put it 
on a rod and test it out?

00:05:33.830 --> 00:05:36.210
It feels a lot different 
than a normal one.

00:05:36.210 --> 00:05:37.230
No, it's okay.

00:05:37.230 --> 00:05:38.650
It's far out of my budget.

00:05:39.240 --> 00:05:41.360
I'm not really going after 
anything that big, either.

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:42.860
Something manual and cheap is fi—

00:05:44.820 --> 00:05:46.740
Otohime

00:05:51.230 --> 00:05:53.200
O-Otohime-sama?

00:05:53.200 --> 00:05:53.910
<i>Gulp.</i>

00:05:54.170 --> 00:05:56.270
I-I get that a lot.

00:05:56.270 --> 00:05:58.220
You actually read this "Otsuki."

00:05:58.220 --> 00:06:02.570
It's not like there'd really be a girl 
from the Ryuuguujou working here.

00:06:04.140 --> 00:06:06.740
Otohime exists, and works 
at a fishing goods store?

00:06:07.950 --> 00:06:09.480
Don't be ridiculous...

00:06:10.410 --> 00:06:11.640
Otohime's whereabouts?

00:06:12.040 --> 00:06:14.970
The Ryuuguujou went out of 
business recently, right?

00:06:14.970 --> 00:06:18.300
I'm just kind of wondering 
where the owner is now.

00:06:19.810 --> 00:06:23.110
Well, it's not like she'd die 
because her castle's gone,

00:06:23.110 --> 00:06:24.610
but any stocks, securities, and the like

00:06:24.610 --> 00:06:26.810
would have been taken
 to pay for her debt,

00:06:26.810 --> 00:06:28.570
so she's got no real assets left.

00:06:28.960 --> 00:06:31.180
She's fallen from high-class.

00:06:31.180 --> 00:06:33.720
I have no clue what she's doing or where.

00:06:33.720 --> 00:06:34.950
I see...

00:06:34.950 --> 00:06:37.200
No hopes or dreams left, huh?

00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:40.750
So why did you ask about 
Otohime all of a sudden?

00:06:43.860 --> 00:06:45.630
Oh, krill!

00:06:45.880 --> 00:06:50.090
<b>Bait & Tackle Period</b>

00:06:51.430 --> 00:06:52.580
Excuse me...

00:06:52.580 --> 00:06:53.430
Welcome—

00:06:54.280 --> 00:06:56.510
Sorry, but do you have 
any rods like this one?

00:06:56.510 --> 00:06:58.650
This one's gotten pretty beaten up.

00:06:58.650 --> 00:07:00.890
We have some for rock 
fishing over here.

00:07:00.890 --> 00:07:02.400
Thanks.

00:07:03.300 --> 00:07:05.560
I'm into levee fishing myself.

00:07:05.560 --> 00:07:06.120
Sorry?

00:07:06.410 --> 00:07:09.580
I caught an oarfish on one.

00:07:09.580 --> 00:07:12.100
Oh, yeah, that loser.

00:07:12.100 --> 00:07:13.660
<i>H-Hey...</i>

00:07:14.260 --> 00:07:16.360
Hm? You're not surprised?

00:07:16.360 --> 00:07:17.120
Huh?

00:07:17.580 --> 00:07:20.830
I believe oarfish are pretty rare.

00:07:22.170 --> 00:07:24.830
Well, you know? You see 
them a lot on the news.

00:07:24.830 --> 00:07:27.040
It's a deep water fish, but 
they get fished up a lot.

00:07:27.040 --> 00:07:28.240
So, you know...

00:07:28.240 --> 00:07:31.380
One of my friends knows 
a lot about the sea.

00:07:33.370 --> 00:07:35.290
I heard that the Ryuuguujou 
went out of business

00:07:35.290 --> 00:07:37.160
and there's just a stone marker left there.

00:07:37.160 --> 00:07:37.960
Gulp!

00:07:37.960 --> 00:07:40.140
I heard that Urashima Taro 
had his life ruined, too.

00:07:40.140 --> 00:07:40.940
Gulp! Gulp!

00:07:40.940 --> 00:07:42.940
And that no one currently knows where

00:07:42.940 --> 00:07:44.420
Otohime-sama is, now that 
she's lost everything.

00:07:44.420 --> 00:07:45.700
Gulp! Gulp! Gulp!

00:07:45.700 --> 00:07:48.010
She said quite a bit.

00:07:48.660 --> 00:07:51.400
How much do you know?

00:07:51.820 --> 00:07:52.700
About what?

00:07:52.550 --> 00:07:53.360
Huh?

00:07:52.700 --> 00:07:53.360
Huh?

00:07:53.620 --> 00:07:55.960
The Ryuuguujou? Otohime-sama?

00:07:55.960 --> 00:07:58.580
She was obviously just 
spouting nonsense.

00:07:59.550 --> 00:08:01.050
<i>Sometimes when you go fishing,</i>

00:08:01.050 --> 00:08:04.080
<i>the door to another world 
is flung open in your face.</i>

00:08:04.080 --> 00:08:06.160
Maybe I'll pick up some sinkers, too.

00:08:05.140 --> 00:08:07.590
<i>But I knew...</i>

00:08:06.160 --> 00:08:08.840
One round split-shot sinker, one barrel sinker...

00:08:09.620 --> 00:08:12.310
<i>There are things in this world that</i>

00:08:12.310 --> 00:08:14.260
<i>it's best not to get too involved in.</i>

00:08:14.260 --> 00:08:15.710
Muromi-san!

00:08:16.260 --> 00:08:18.220
<b>One week later</b>

00:08:16.610 --> 00:08:18.220
What are you after?!

00:08:18.580 --> 00:08:20.180
What do you want?!

00:08:21.040 --> 00:08:24.060
I'd like to use this to catch 
some Japanese whiting.

00:08:24.060 --> 00:08:25.770
<b>Japanese whiting</b>

00:08:24.060 --> 00:08:25.770
<b>(Sillaginidae Family)</b>

00:08:24.060 --> 00:08:25.770
<b>Often found near sandy waters throughout Japan.</b>

00:08:25.770 --> 00:08:26.990
Don't try to change the subject!

00:08:26.990 --> 00:08:28.440
You know everything, don't you?!

00:08:28.440 --> 00:08:30.820
You keep coming to my store, 
knowing about my past!

00:08:30.820 --> 00:08:32.150
I know you're planning something!

00:08:32.150 --> 00:08:33.420
<i>I'm kinda stuck here.</i>

00:08:32.260 --> 00:08:35.110
Always thinks someone's out to get her.

00:08:33.420 --> 00:08:35.750
<i>The only fishing goods shop in 
the neighborhood is this one.</i>

00:08:35.750 --> 00:08:37.550
Hm? What are you talking about?

00:08:37.550 --> 00:08:38.830
Stop trying to trick me!

00:08:38.830 --> 00:08:40.180
I can't take this anymore!

00:08:40.180 --> 00:08:42.340
These past few days, 
I've been dreaming that

00:08:42.340 --> 00:08:44.170
you go around telling 
people who I really am!

00:08:44.170 --> 00:08:45.790
<i>She's acting like she's 
some sort of fugitive.</i>

00:08:45.790 --> 00:08:48.480
I'd feel a lot better if you just 
blackmailed me already! So do it!

00:08:48.480 --> 00:08:50.560
What do you want? You want money?!

00:08:50.560 --> 00:08:51.870
Huh? What is it?

00:08:50.670 --> 00:08:52.920
I just want some fish hooks...

00:08:51.870 --> 00:08:55.510
If you're gonna do something, don't 
drag it out, just freaking do it!

00:08:56.360 --> 00:08:59.240
<i>I think avoiding this any longer 
is going to be difficult.</i>

00:08:59.240 --> 00:09:00.220
<i>Guess I have no choice.</i>

00:09:00.690 --> 00:09:01.470
Otohime-san...

00:09:01.470 --> 00:09:02.450
Yes?

00:09:02.450 --> 00:09:04.520
When does your shift end?

00:09:05.150 --> 00:09:07.600
Pretty soon, I guess...

00:09:07.960 --> 00:09:08.980
I see.

00:09:09.340 --> 00:09:13.780
Then, I'd like to take you somewhere.
 Come with me after this.

00:09:13.780 --> 00:09:15.040
O-Okay...

00:09:15.870 --> 00:09:17.200
<i>This will work.</i>

00:09:17.200 --> 00:09:19.120
<i>Now I'll be free of all this.</i>

00:09:19.120 --> 00:09:21.050
<i>Yes, free.</i>

00:09:21.050 --> 00:09:23.830
Um, where are we going?

00:09:24.550 --> 00:09:26.000
We're almost there.

00:09:26.420 --> 00:09:27.440
Right.

00:09:28.510 --> 00:09:31.170
There aren't many people around here.

00:09:31.600 --> 00:09:32.050
Huh?

00:09:32.580 --> 00:09:33.760
N-Nothing...

00:09:35.170 --> 00:09:36.970
<i>W-Wait...</i>

00:09:37.150 --> 00:09:39.430
<i>He's not going to violate me, is he?!</i>

00:09:39.430 --> 00:09:41.670
N-No! Not outside!

00:09:42.850 --> 00:09:43.780
Otohime-san?

00:09:44.400 --> 00:09:45.240
Otohime-san?

00:09:45.240 --> 00:09:47.230
Wait! My heart isn't prepared for this!

00:09:48.090 --> 00:09:50.990
This is the girl who told 
me about the Ryuuguujou.

00:09:58.490 --> 00:09:59.530
You fish monster!

00:09:59.530 --> 00:10:00.740
You're the witch of the deep!

00:10:00.740 --> 00:10:03.010
Takkun, why are you with this wench?!

00:10:03.010 --> 00:10:06.320
This girl's crazy! She kidnaps men 
and sucks out their life force!

00:10:06.320 --> 00:10:07.410
That's not true!

00:10:07.410 --> 00:10:08.600
You're always going around

00:10:08.600 --> 00:10:09.940
spreading rumors that make me look bad!

00:10:09.940 --> 00:10:11.620
You're rattling my brains!

00:10:11.620 --> 00:10:13.840
You stupid trout! You've been 
fishing up too many lies!

00:10:14.400 --> 00:10:15.300
Like the fish you are.

00:10:24.120 --> 00:10:26.240
You're dislocating my joints!

00:10:27.280 --> 00:10:29.440
It's been a while since I felt this.

00:10:29.440 --> 00:10:31.390
What's with the dumpy outfit?

00:10:31.390 --> 00:10:33.100
You've fallen pretty far.

00:10:33.100 --> 00:10:34.530
All those nights of partying and debauchery

00:10:34.530 --> 00:10:35.810
finally came back to haunt you?

00:10:35.810 --> 00:10:37.690
Call it show business! 
It was show business!

00:10:37.690 --> 00:10:39.630
I ended up going out of 
business because you guys

00:10:39.630 --> 00:10:42.280
spread all of those baseless rumors, 
causing my ticket sales to drop!

00:10:42.600 --> 00:10:43.620
Death at sea.

00:10:43.620 --> 00:10:44.990
Take this!

00:10:46.690 --> 00:10:47.670
My joints!

00:10:47.670 --> 00:10:48.960
It's been a while...

00:10:48.960 --> 00:10:51.320
What's with you?!

00:10:51.320 --> 00:10:54.210
I guess they have a relationship 
like chlorine and acid.

00:10:54.230 --> 00:10:55.700
<b>Don't mix these.</b>

00:10:54.530 --> 00:10:55.710
This is serious.

00:10:56.620 --> 00:10:58.160
This is over.

00:10:58.160 --> 00:10:59.550
That's all for today!

00:11:01.160 --> 00:11:03.590
I only brought you here 
today to clear up your

00:11:03.590 --> 00:11:05.330
misunderstanding about me, Otohime.

00:11:05.330 --> 00:11:07.540
So why don't you go on home?

00:11:07.540 --> 00:11:09.560
Sure. Got it.

00:11:09.850 --> 00:11:13.120
Takkun, why are you getting 
so close to Otohime?

00:11:13.120 --> 00:11:14.850
We're not really close.

00:11:14.850 --> 00:11:17.190
She just works at the fishing 
goods store I go to a lot.

00:11:17.190 --> 00:11:20.120
Anyway, you shouldn't get 
too involved with her.

00:11:20.120 --> 00:11:22.680
Nothing good will come of 
getting close to that witch.

00:11:22.680 --> 00:11:25.700
She might seem nice at first glance, 
but she's a terrible person...

00:11:26.060 --> 00:11:28.570
She always looks down on 
people and laughs at them.

00:11:28.570 --> 00:11:30.640
Her flashy outfit was an eyesore, too.

00:11:30.640 --> 00:11:31.700
Actually, this one time...

00:11:31.700 --> 00:11:32.810
Hey, are you listening?

00:11:32.810 --> 00:11:35.390
You need to listen to 
me. This is important.

00:11:35.390 --> 00:11:36.860
You understand, don't you?

00:11:36.860 --> 00:11:38.880
You need to stop hanging 
out with mermaids.

00:11:38.880 --> 00:11:40.680
She's always going on 
about stupid things.

00:11:40.680 --> 00:11:42.320
I mean, the reason why the Ryuuguujou

00:11:42.320 --> 00:11:43.880
started to have problems was because

